./configure --cfgfile=cfgchiara.txt





Here some instructions and tricks
1) old vs new code is a compile-time choice: OLDCODE=true/false in the cfg file
   (default false = general code). The old code is Z only.
   [useful for debugging]

2) the boson is chosen at run time: -boson z / wm / wp (default z)
   z : Z boson, wm : W- exchange, wp : W+ exchange
   -----> the analysis (compile time, analysis= in the cfg file) has to be set accordingly

  (?) whay to set automatically the correct analysis?  

3) The order of the partons is always: q qp > l lx
   namely: d ux > w- > e- vex
           dx u > w+ > ve e+




